      {
        "id": "entry-fast-paths",
        "fact": "Before commander: when any argv token is logs|attach|stop|kill|respawn|rm, backgroundSessionVerbIndex(argv, {behindRootOptions: CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_KIND !== \"bg\"}) decides whether it is a background verb (background-verb-index); --bg/--background dispatch only through hasBackgroundFlag (background-flag-value-aware); either path refuses --desktop. remote-control|rc|remote|sync|bridge and self-hosted-runner still dispatch as argv[0] only, daemon after any --dangerously-skip-permissions/--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions, and the version fast path is an argv of exactly --version|-v|-V (with --verbose).",
        "anchorSha256": "e1085f941cfa375cec11bf9f91dafc320a37843069ff74c68d3f69067f0b2b43",
        "anchorBytes": 139,
        "anchorByteOffset": 217069106,
        "windowStart": 217067058,
        "windowBytes": 8192,
        "windowSha256": "20ed335062a6752b16b9f079d292992de87692e02b0f5381d369a0f546e7c9a3"
      },
      {
        "id": "background-verb-index",
        "fact": "A background verb is the first operand (value-aware; after `--` the next token is the operand). At argv[0] it always dispatches. Behind other tokens it dispatches only when behindRootOptions holds (not inside a bg session), the verb does not directly follow `--`, the next token is an 8-hex job id (or respawn --all), and every preceding token is a safe root option (boolean flags such as --verbose, or a value option outside --exec|-m|--handle-uri); -p/--print, --bg, --routine, help, version and short clusters disqualify it. Otherwise the verb is an ordinary operand (a prompt).",
        "anchorSha256": "dfd61da87aa4a6424a6f6b9500c41a6abbde2b72efc6481c2af0a856d125a471",
        "anchorBytes": 110,
        "anchorByteOffset": 218578382,
